      "note": "The four classes in the model rule are examples. Count desmopressin once when co-prescribed in a qualifying formulation. These include oral desmopressin, Minirin nasal spray and documented Minirin or Octostim injection, which carry low-sodium warnings. Use the recorded product and route. A separate procedure or an earlier single dose without co-treatment does not qualify. Count hydrochlorothiazide in a single or combination product once. Count sodium valproate and valproic acid as one valproate medicine, including when both names match Epilim. Count indapamide once whether supplied alone or in a combination."
    }
  ],
  "rule_for_models": "Suspect a finding when the person is aged 65 or over and the history shows a supply of a Group A medicine (an SSRI) or an A2 medicine (an SNRI) together with supplies of at least two different Group B medicines (including the listed diuretics, antipsychotics, anticonvulsants, proton pump inhibitors and qualifying desmopressin formulations in Group B), all with supply dates that overlap or fall within 60 days of each other. Exclude a combination when a recorded stop or switch shows the antidepressant and both partners were never used together. If this medicine pattern is present and age is unknown, report a possible finding and name the missing fact Age and ask for age in years. A known age below 65 gives no finding.",
  "cannot_be_seen": "The person's actual sodium level, whether each medicine is really taken, and other medicines that can lower sodium.",
  "ask_the_gp": "A serum sodium check and a review of whether all of these medicines are still needed.",
  "urgency": "routine",
